course: dictionary
lesson: 13640
title: Words for things that must happen
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Inevitability is a noun. It names a thing: the fact that something is certain to happen and cannot be avoided. Its root word is inevitable, which also means «certain to happen». When you meet inevitability, ask yourself: will this happen no matter what? If yes, the word fits.
explain: «Getting older is an inevitability for everyone.» Nobody can stop their birthdays from coming, so ageing is certain. Try the swap test: put «something certain to happen» in place of inevitability. «Getting older is something certain to happen for everyone» still makes sense, so you have found the right meaning.
explain: Stories and sums use it too. «As the bridge creaked, the readers felt the inevitability of the crash.» The readers know the crash is coming, and that feeling builds the tension. In maths, a dice always shows a number from 1 to 6, so «rolling a number under 7 is an inevitability», because it is certain.
fact: Inevitability means the fact that something is certain to happen and cannot be avoided.
fact: An inevitability is one particular thing that will surely happen.
fact: «Inevitability» is a noun, and its plural is «inevitabilities».
fact: The adjective «inevitable» means certain to happen and impossible to avoid.
fact: In science, the seasons and the tides are inevitabilities because of how the Earth moves.
exercise: «Night will follow day, and that is an inevitability.» What does inevitability mean here? | A bright light in the sky | A wish that someone makes | Something that might happen, or might not | *Something certain to happen and impossible to avoid
exercise: The storm was coming, and the crew felt the inevitability of the wreck. Which phrase could replace inevitability? | Something that is always late | A kind of storm | A secret that nobody knows | *Something certain to happen
exercise: «Rolling a number under 7 on a dice is an inevitability.» Why is this an inevitability? | *Because every dice roll must land on 1 to 6 | Because dice are fun to play with | Because some rolls are lucky | Because it is a rare event
test: «Ageing and death are inevitabilities in life.» What is an inevitability? | A kind of game | *Something that will surely happen | A wish you make on a birthday | A rare event that never happens
test: What is the plural of inevitability? | inevitably | *inevitabilities | inevitabilitys | inevitable
exam: Which sentence uses inevitability correctly? | Let us have an inevitability for lunch | The inevitability is a kind of blue paint | I hope it is an inevitability that I win the prize | *Seasons are an inevitability because of how the Earth moves
